# quest/029/StmBdb108_02969 — «A Sultana's Resolve» · in play order
msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Language: ru\n"
"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\n"
"X-Game-Version: 2026.09.15.0000.0000\n"
"X-Source-Language: en\n"

#. ja: ゴールドソーサーのナナモ・ウル・ナモは、考え直しているようだ。
#. de: Sultana Nanamo ist nachdenklich geworden.
#. fr: Le cerveau de Nanamo est en ébullition.
#. kind: journal
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_SEQ_00:1"
msgid "Nanamo appears to be reassessing her plans."
msgstr ""

#. ja: クガネのハンコックと話す
#. de: In Kugane mit Hancock sprechen
#. fr: Parler à Hancock, à Kugane
#. kind: objective
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_TODO_00:1"
msgid "Speak with Hancock in Kugane."
msgstr ""

#. ja: ウルダハのナナモ・ウル・ナモと話す
#. de: In Ul'dah mit Nanamo Ul Namo sprechen
#. fr: Parler à Nanamo, à Ul'dah
#. kind: objective
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_TODO_01:1"
msgid "Speak with Nanamo in Ul'dah."
msgstr ""

#. ja: 砂の家のナナモ・ウル・ナモと話す
#. de: Im Sonnenwind mit Nanamo Ul Namo sprechen
#. fr: Parler à Nanamo, au Refuge des sables
#. kind: objective
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_TODO_02:1"
msgid "Speak with Nanamo at the Waking Sands."
msgstr ""

#. ja: ナナモ・ウル・ナモと再度話す
#. de: Erneut mit Nanamo Ul Namo sprechen
#. fr: Reparler à Nanamo
#. kind: objective
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_TODO_03:1"
msgid "Speak with Nanamo."
msgstr ""

#. ja: ウルダハの利益か……<br>わらわも、まだまだ考えが浅かったということじゃな。
#. de: Godbert hat Recht. Unser Kapital muss auch Ul'dah zugutekommen. Ich hatte da einfach nicht weit genug gedacht.
#. fr: Quelque chose de bénéfique à Ul'dah... Je me rends compte à quel point j'ai été naïve.
#. speaker: NANAMOULNAMO
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_NANAMOULNAMO_000_001:1"
msgid "<i>Profit</i>... The thought never even crossed my mind."
msgstr ""

#. ja: しかし、己の浅はかさを嘆いてはおれぬ。<br>学びを得て、前進あるのみじゃ！
#. de: Zum Glück ist es noch nicht zu spät, den Plan zu verfeinern, und ich lasse mich gerne beraten. Es ist keine Schande, manchmal den Überblick zu verlieren, solange man sein Ziel nicht aus den Augen verliert.
#. fr: Mais rien ne sert de me lamenter sur mon manque d'expérience. Je dois apprendre petit à petit<nbsp>!
#. speaker: NANAMOULNAMO
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_NANAMOULNAMO_000_002:1"
msgid "But standing about lamenting my naivety will not do anyone any good. I shall consider my lesson learned, and press on."
msgstr ""

#. ja: ところで、<split " " 1><string $gs1></split>よ、<br>そなたの知り合いに、熟練の商人はおらぬか？<br>利益の上げ方について尋ねるなら、商人を置いてほかになかろう。
#. de: <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>, kennst du nicht einen erfahrenen Händler? Händler wissen doch am besten, wie man klug investiert, um Gewinne zu erwirtschaften.
#. fr: Au fait, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>, n'as-tu pas des marchands parmi tes con<shy>nais<shy>san<shy>ces<nbsp>? C'est exactement le genre de personne qui saurait me dire comment faire en sorte que mon projet génère des profits.
#. speaker: NANAMOULNAMO
#. macro: <split " " 1><string $gs1></split> — the first name of the player character (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <string $gs1> — a text value passed to the string; value = global text 1 (the name of the player character) (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_NANAMOULNAMO_000_003:1"
msgid "<split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>─are you perchance acquainted with any successful merchants? If my attempt at philanthropy is obliged to reap a profit, it would seem wise to consult someone with a knack for business."
msgstr ""

#. ja: ふむ、クガネにて、東アルデナード商会の番頭に世話になったと。<br>ならば、その「ハンコック」とやらに、<br>協力を仰いできてはもらえぬだろうか？
#. de: Ah, der Prokurist der Ostaldenard-Handelsgesellschaft in Kugane. Kannst du diesen Hancock um Rat fragen?
#. fr: Le tabellion de la Firme du commerce de l'Aldenard oriental à Kugane, dis-tu<nbsp>? Ce Hancock pourrait avoir le savoir et les compétences qui me manquent, en effet. Son aide me serait très précieuse...
#. speaker: NANAMOULNAMO
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_NANAMOULNAMO_000_004:1"
msgid "Hm... Ordinarily, I would not trust any agent of the East Aldenard Trading Company─but if you hold this Hancock fellow in high esteem, I am content to be led by you. You may repay my faith by journeying to distant Kugane and speaking with him on my behalf."
msgstr ""

#. ja: さすがに、わらわは国外に出るわけにもゆかぬ。<br>手数をかけるが、後ほどウルダハのエーテライト・プラザ近くで、<br>合流するとしよう……それではな！
#. de: Ich würde ja gerne selbst mit ihm reden, aber ich kann Thanalan nicht ohne Weiteres verlassen. Ich erwarte deine Rückkehr am Ätherytenplatz. Gute Reise!
#. fr: Mal<shy>heu<shy>reu<shy>se<shy>ment, il m'est impossible d'aller à l'étranger. Je suis désolée de te demander ça, mais pourrais-tu le contacter de ma part, s'il te plaît<nbsp>? Nous n'aurons qu'à nous retrouver près de la place de l'Éthérite d'Ul'dah ensuite. À plus tard, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split><nbsp>!
#. speaker: NANAMOULNAMO
#. macro: <split " " 1><string $gs1></split> — the first name of the player character (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <string $gs1> — a text value passed to the string; value = global text 1 (the name of the player character) (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_NANAMOULNAMO_000_005:1"
msgid "Eager though I am to visit those shores, I have not the leisure for a lengthy sea voyage. Now, assuming you will travel as adventurers are wont to do, I shall await your report by the aetheryte in Ul'dah. A fair journey to you, <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>─and a <i>swift</i> one, if you please."
msgstr ""

#. ja: オォ～、これは、これは、お久しぶりデ～ス。<br>今日は、どういったご用件で？
#. de: Oh, welch ehrenwerter Besuch! Was kann ich dieses Mal für Euch tun?
#. fr: Oh, quel plaisir de vous revoir, <if $gn4>ma chère<else>mon cher</if> <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>. Dites-moi, quel bon vent vous amène<nbsp>?
#. speaker: HANCOCK
#. macro: <split " " 1><string $gs1></split> — the first name of the player character (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <string $gs1> — a text value passed to the string; value = global text 1 (the name of the player character) (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_HANCOCK_000_010:1"
msgid "<split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>! To what do I owe the pleasure? Or are you here on business?"
msgstr ""

#. ja: ナナモ様が、アラミゴ難民の帰国支援のため、<br>商人の助言を求めておられる……と。
#. de: Sultana Nanamo möchte die Flüchtlinge bei ihrer Rückkehr unterstützen und sucht für diese Unternehmung den Rat eines erfahrenen Geschäftsmanns?
#. fr: Comment<nbsp>? Sa Majesté Nanamo souhaite que je lui donne des conseils<nbsp>?
#. speaker: HANCOCK
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_HANCOCK_000_011:1"
msgid "...I beg your pardon? Her Grace the sultana would have <i>my</i> opinion on how best to invest the wealth of Ul'dah?"
msgstr ""

#. ja: 実に興味深い話デスが、<split " " 1><string $gs1></split>さん、<br>来るところを間違えてマ～ス！
#. de: <if $gn4>Verehrte<else>Verehrter</if> <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>, das klingt höchst interessant, aber mit Verlaub, Ihr habt Euch an den Falschen gewandt.
#. fr: C'est un grand honneur, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>, mais je crains que la Sultane ne se trompe d'interlocuteur<nbsp>!
#. speaker: HANCOCK
#. macro: <split " " 1><string $gs1></split> — the first name of the player character (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <string $gs1> — a text value passed to the string; value = global text 1 (the name of the player character) (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_HANCOCK_000_012:1"
msgid "My dear <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>... I have you to thank for this...recognition, I am sure. And I am flattered that you came to me. Truly flattered."
msgstr ""

#. ja: アナタ方が相談すべきは、小物に過ぎない私などではなく、<br>東アルデナード商会の会長、ロロリトその人であるべきデ～ス！<br>「百億ギルの男」に勝る商人など、いませんからネ。
#. de: Meine Wenigkeit ist doch bloß ein kleines Rad im Getriebe. Ihr solltet Euch direkt an den Steuermann wenden, den Vorsitzenden der Ostaldenard-Handelsgesellschaft.
#. fr: Je n'ai que très peu d'importance, voyez-vous, et à mon avis, notre président, le seigneur Lolorito, est assurément la personne la mieux placée pour répondre à toutes les interrogations de Sa Majesté. Ce n'est pas pour rien qu'on le surnomme “le milliardaire”<nbsp>!
#. speaker: HANCOCK
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_HANCOCK_000_013:1"
msgid "But why settle for a lowly apprentice, when you could have the master! Upon matters of profit, there is no living soul better-qualified to advise Her Grace than Chairman Lolorito─a man whose morning “exertions” are said to fill his garderobe with gold!"
msgstr ""

#. ja: 私の方から、会長に取り次いでおきますから、<br>「暁」のザナラーンにおける拠点で、交渉するのデ～ス！<br>手強い相手デスが、ご武運をお祈りしていますヨ？
#. de: Ich werde Lolorito umgehend über das Ansinnen der Sultana informieren und schlage vor, die Verhandlung in Thanalan zu führen. Herr Lolorito ist gewiss kein leichter Ver<shy>handlungs<shy>partner, aber er lässt über alles mit sich reden. Viel Erfolg!
#. fr: Je vais me charger de le contacter pour vous et d'arranger un rendez-vous... hmmm, disons aux locaux des Héritiers dans le Thanalan<nbsp>! J'espère que la Sultane et vous-même obtiendrez ce que vous souhaitez de cet échange<nbsp>! Je suis de tout cœur avec vous, en tout cas<nbsp>!
#. speaker: HANCOCK
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: <split " " 1><string $gs1></split> — the first name of the player character (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <string $gs1> — a text value passed to the string; value = global text 1 (the name of the player character) (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_HANCOCK_000_014:1"
msgid "I should be happy to arrange a meeting for you...say, at the Scions' former headquarters in Thanalan? The Waking Sands would seem a suitably <i>neutral</i> venue for negotiations, don't you think? Fare you well, <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>, and may your dealings prove fruitful!"
msgstr ""

#. ja: 本当に利益を得たいのなら、<br>「百億ギルの男」を、味方に付けるのデ～ス！<br>ン～、楽しくなってきましたネ！
#. de: Niemand hat ein besseres Gespür für lohnende Geschäfte als Lolorito. Ich bin gespannt, was Sultana Nanamo und er gemeinsam aushecken werden.
#. fr: Si la Sultane souhaite faire de son projet une affaire profitable, elle a tout intérêt à faire du seigneur Lolorito son allié<nbsp>! Quoi qu'il en soit, toute cette histoire m'a l'air pas<shy>sion<shy>nan<shy>te<nbsp>! Je suis de tout cœur avec vous<nbsp>!
#. speaker: HANCOCK
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_HANCOCK_000_015:1"
msgid "You will not find a shrewder merchant than Chairman Lolorito. Would that I could be present to witness the back-and-forth of your coming negotiations!"
msgstr ""

#. ja: 戻ったか、<split " " 1><string $gs1></split>。<br>それで、ハンコックの協力は得られたのか？
#. de: <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>, willkommen zurück! Konntest du Hancock überzeugen, uns zu helfen?
#. fr: Ah, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split><nbsp>! J'attendais ton retour avec impatience<nbsp>! As-tu réussi à obtenir l'aide de Hancock<nbsp>?
#. speaker: NANAMOULNAMO
#. macro: <split " " 1><string $gs1></split> — the first name of the player character (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <string $gs1> — a text value passed to the string; value = global text 1 (the name of the player character) (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_NANAMOULNAMO_000_020:1"
msgid "Welcome back, <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>. Did your merchant friend have any useful advice to share?"
msgstr ""

#. ja: な、なんと……ロロリトとの交渉を提案されたと！？
#. de: Oje, wir sollen direkt mit Lolorito verhandeln?!
#. fr: Comment<nbsp>!? Demander conseil au seigneur Lolorito<nbsp>!?
#. speaker: NANAMOULNAMO
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_NANAMOULNAMO_000_021:1"
msgid "...With <i>Lolorito</i>!? And you agreed to this!?"
msgstr ""

#. ja: ……確かに利益を上げることにかけては、<br>ヤツに勝る者など、このウルダハにはおるまい……。<br>だが、ロロリトが共和派の筆頭であることは…………
#. de: Sicher, er ist ohne Zweifel der erfolgreichste Geschäftsmann von Ul'dah, doch leider auch der Ränkeschmied der Republikaner.
#. fr: Il n'y a en effet personne de plus compétent que lui pour m'aider dans mon projet... Mais c'est également le chef de file des monétaristes...
#. speaker: NANAMOULNAMO
#. macro: <i> — italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
#. macro: </i> — end of: italic text (formatting: keep it as often as the source has it)
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_NANAMOULNAMO_000_022:1"
msgid "I am well aware of his standing in the field of business. But I had hoped to keep the Monetarists at arm's length, and <i>him</i> in particular..."
msgstr ""

#. ja: いや、これは砂の女王として、避けては通れぬ道か……。<br>ロロリトをも使いこなせずして、ウルダハを導くことなどできぬ！
#. de: Nun ... ich fürchte, es führt kein Weg an ihm vorbei. Um Ul'dah zu führen, muss es mir gelingen, Lolorito für meine Zwecke einzuspannen.
#. fr: Mais qu'est-ce que je raconte<nbsp>!? Si je veux assumer pleinement mon rôle de sultane, je dois absolument savoir traiter habilement avec des gens comme Lolorito<nbsp>!
#. speaker: NANAMOULNAMO
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_NANAMOULNAMO_000_023:1"
msgid "...Nay. I cannot live in fear of the man. I must learn how to treat with him if I am to rule Ul'dah effectively."
msgstr ""

#. ja: わらわは、覚悟を決めたぞ、<split " " 1><string $gs1></split>！<br>すまぬが「砂の家」を、交渉の場とさせてもらいたい！<br>ウルダハとアラミゴの未来のため、ヤツを説き伏せてみせよう！
#. de: Also gut, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>, ich will versuchen, Lolorito zur Zusammenarbeit zu bewegen - um der Zukunft Ul'dahs und Ala Mhigos willen. Meinst du, der Bund der Morgenröte ist so nett, uns die Verhandlung im Sonnenwind führen zu lassen? Auf neutralem Boden würde ich mich wohler fühlen.
#. fr: Je suis prête, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split><nbsp>! Je vais me rendre au Refuge des sables et négocier avec celui qui a longtemps été mon plus grand ennemi<nbsp>! Il en va du bien d'Ul'dah et d'Ala Mhigo<nbsp>!
#. speaker: NANAMOULNAMO
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_NANAMOULNAMO_000_024:1"
msgid "Very well! I will meet with Lolorito. Let us go on ahead to the Waking Sands, and prepare for his coming."
msgstr ""

#. ja: ここが「暁の血盟」の拠点のひとつ、「砂の家」か……。<br>噂には聞いておったが、訪れるのははじめてのことじゃ。
#. de: Das ist also der Sonnenwind. Ich habe zwar schon viel über ihn gehört, bin aber zum ersten Mal hier.
#. fr: Je crois bien que c'est la première fois que je pénètre dans l'une des bases des Héritiers de la Septième Aube...
#. speaker: NANAMOULNAMO
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_NANAMOULNAMO_000_030:1"
msgid "So this is where the Scions first congregated... I have heard many tales, but never had occasion to visit."
msgstr ""

#. ja: さて、この一室を借りて、ロロリトとの交渉に臨むとしよう。<br>わらわは、少しばかり準備をするゆえ、すまぬが、<br>そなたは人払いの方を頼むぞ？
#. de: Ich bin dem Bund der Morgenröte dankbar, dass er uns einen neutralen Ort zur Verfügung stellt. Würdest du bitte dafür sorgen, dass wir ungestört sind, während ich mich auf die Verhandlung vorbereite?
#. fr: Je pense que cette salle conviendra par<shy>fai<shy>te<shy>ment pour la rencontre avec le seigneur Lolorito. Veux-tu bien demander aux gens qui sont dedans de libérer les lieux pendant que je me prépare, s'il te plaît<nbsp>?
#. speaker: NANAMOULNAMO
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_NANAMOULNAMO_000_031:1"
msgid "To work, then. The hour of the meeting draws near, and I would gather my thoughts. Pray see to it that we have the appointed room to ourselves."
msgstr ""

#. ja: ……ふぅ。<br>このように緊張を強いられる交渉事は、なかなか経験がないぞ。
#. de: Puh, ich war in meinem ganzen Leben selten so nervös wie bei dieser Verhandlung. Lolorito hat es wirklich faustdick hinter den Ohren.
#. fr: Je suis vraiment soulagée que ça soit fini... Je n'avais jamais eu à conduire de telles négociations jusqu'à présent. J'étais vraiment tendue.
#. speaker: NANAMOULNAMO
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_NANAMOULNAMO_000_040:1"
msgid "\\<sigh> I fear it will be many years before I feel comfortable taking part in such negotiations."
msgstr ""

#. ja: しかし、そなたが横にいてくれたおかげで、<br>どうにかロロリトから協力を取り付けることができた。<br>感謝するぞ、<split " " 1><string $gs1></split>。
#. de: Gut, dass du bei mir warst. Dadurch habe ich mich sicherer gefühlt und konnte Lolorito überzeugen. Vielen Dank, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>!
#. fr: C'est en grande partie parce que tu étais là, à mes côtés, que j'ai réussi à obtenir de Lolorito qu'il m'aide pour mon projet. Je t'en suis ex<shy>trê<shy>me<shy>ment re<shy>con<shy>nais<shy>sante, <split " " 1><string $gs1></split>.
#. speaker: NANAMOULNAMO
#. macro: <br> — a line break (may be added or dropped)
#. macro: <split " " 1><string $gs1></split> — the first name of the player character (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
#. macro: <string $gs1> — a text value passed to the string; value = global text 1 (the name of the player character) (game data: keep it; it may move or repeat)
msgctxt "quest/029/StmBdb108_02969:TEXT_STMBDB108_02969_NANAMOULNAMO_000_041:1"
msgid "But I shall not complain. We have piqued Lolorito's interest and secured his invaluable expertise.<br>Thank you, <split \" \" 1><string $gs1></split>. I could not have done it without you."
msgstr ""
